FWIW, I think you may be able to run more shorter chains without thinning if you use non centered random effects. Instead of:

for (i in 1:I) {
  x[i] ~ dnorm(0, tau)
}

where tau is precision do

for (i in 1:I) {
  x[i] <- sigma * z[i]
  z[i] ~ dnorm(0, 1)
}

Where sigma is the SD.

