Dear all,

in June 2026, Michael Schaub and I are going to teach a 5-day Bayesian modeling workshop at the University of Debrecen, Hungary:

Bayesian occupancy, N-mixture and population modelling using NIMBLE and JAGS

The workshop will contain a gentle introduction to Bayesian inference and computation, focusing on the two software products that we think currently have the best tradeoff between user-friendliness and power and flexibility. Thus, we will use JAGS and NIMBLE to fit and understand some of the most widely used models for the analysis of animal and plant populations. Models and topics include:

GLMs and generalized linear mixed models
Site-occupancy models
N-mixture models
State-space models
Cormack-Jolly-Seber models
Multistate capture-recapture models
Advanced use of NIMBLE (e.g. use of nimble functions, MCMC configuration)
The joy of data simulation
General integrated and integrated population models (IPMs)
Debrecen can be easily reached from the capital Budapest via public transport or rental car, and Hungary has very much indeed to offer for vacationers, both 'traditional' and more bird or other nature-oriented. For instance, it is right next to the famous Hortobagy National Park.

Please send your application to Michael Schaub (michael...@vogelwarte.ch), with cc to Zoltán Németh (nemeth...@science.unideb.hu), describing your background and knowledge in statistical modelling, R and NIMBLE/JAGS, by 25 February 2026 at the latest.

Best regards  --- M & M

